{"id":31425,"title":"Plane parallel radiance transport for global illumination in vegetation","url":"https://www.osti.gov/biblio/649229","final_url":"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/649229","year":1997,"kind":"paper","source":"osti","doi":"10.1007/978-3-7091-6858-5_22","arxiv":null,"sha256":"5c2d9dfe2efdbbf351ed756cbce5cd2e6a179113be033e52b71eb12f470de512","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"oa","fetched_at":1793062253.403393,"text_chars":41848,"abstract":"This paper applies plane parallel radiance transport techniques to scattering from vegetation. The leaves, stems, and branches are represented as a volume density of scattering surfaces, depending only on height and the vertical component of the surface normal. Ordinary differential equations are written for the multiply scattered radiance as a function of the height above the ground, with the sky radiance and ground reflectance as boundary conditions. They are solved using a two-pass integration scheme to unify the two-point boundary conditions, and Fourier series for the dependence on the azimuthal angle. The resulting radiance distribution is used to precompute diffuse and specular `ambient` shading tables, as a function of height and surface normal, to be used in rendering, together with a z-buffer shadow algorithm for direct solar illumination.","file":null,"marks":["book"],"links":["https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/649229","https://www.osti.gov/biblio/649229","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc703463/m2/1/high_res_d/649229.pdf","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc703463/?q=volume rendering equation","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc703463/?q=volume illumination","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc703463/?q=optical models for direct volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc703463/?q=ambient occlusion volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc703463/?q=precomputed radiance transfer volume","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc703463/?q=multiple scattering rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc703463/?q=local illumination volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc703463/?q=single scattering volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc703463/?q=light transport participating media","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc703463/?q=precomputed transfer volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc703463/?q=phong lighting model volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc703463/?q=diffuse global illumination sky sampling","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc703463/?q=fourier volume resampling","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc703463/?q=hemisphere sampling global illumination","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc703463/?q=sky radiance model","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc703463/?q=precomputed multiple scattering table","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc703463/?q=point-based global illumination participating media","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc703463/?q=precomputed single scattering"],"cited_by":[{"path":"20161-hierarchical-depth-map-rendering.md","name":"Hierarchical Depth Map Rendering","k":2},{"path":"20250-plane-parallel-radiance-transport-for-vegetation.md","name":"Plane Parallel Radiance Transport for Vegetation","k":1},{"path":"20199-riccati-equation-for-boundary-conditions.md","name":"Riccati Equation for Boundary Conditions","k":1},{"path":"23029-phong-brdf-with-precomputed-integrals.md","name":"Phong BRDF with Precomputed Integrals","k":1},{"path":"20187-analytical-integration-of-scattering-phase-function-for-rand.md","name":"Analytical Integration of Scattering Phase Function for Random Polygons","k":1},{"path":"20230-extinction-coefficient-computation.md","name":"Extinction Coefficient Computation","k":1}]}